; A Java statement expression discards the reviewed return value of an
; exact JDK 21 String.trim() call. Python's arm uses the reviewed CPython /
; typeshed str transformation set under the explicitly stated builtin-receiver
; assumption. Rust's native arm covers a discarded call whose resolved
; callable or workspace return type carries exact `must_use`. C and C++ cover
; a discarded call whose resolved declaration or workspace result type carries
; native [[nodiscard]] or GNU warn_unused_result evidence. The
; call-result-obligations relation checks every feasible dispatch arm before a
; finding. An ordinary Python assignment, including `_ = s.strip()`, consumes
; the value and is not a discard.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.correctness.discarded-pure-result"
  :name "Discarded pure transformation result"
  :message "the result of this reviewed pure transformation or must-use value is discarded"
  :severity warning
  :description "The exact JDK 21 String.trim() return value is unused by an expression statement or for-loop initializer/update. Python's reviewed CPython/typeshed str.strip, lower, upper, and two-argument replace values are unused by a direct expression statement under the stated assumption that annotated or inferred builtins.str receivers use the builtin implementation and builtin methods are not replaced; str subclasses and unknown or union receiver flows remain incomplete. An ordinary Python assignment, including `_ = s.strip()`, is consumption rather than discard. An expression lambda also discards the result when its resolved functional method returns void; a value-returning target retains it. Rust calls whose resolved declaration or workspace return type carries exact built-in must_use are covered by the native obligation arm; C and C++ calls use declaration or workspace class/struct/enum [[nodiscard]] and GNU warn_unused_result evidence read from attribute nodes. std/core must_use types without a reviewed model remain open. Unresolved or conflicting functional contracts, overloads, or native dispatch arms remain incomplete. Classifying a deferred body does not prove that it executes. This diagnostic requires a reviewed pure-transformation or native must_use obligation, proved result use, and complete dispatch coverage. Calls with missing model, artifact, declaration, or attribute evidence remain incomplete."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-code-smell-pack"
  :tags ["correctness" "java" "python" "rust" "c" "cpp" "result-use"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name discarded
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (union
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq pure_transformation_value)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language java
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call :callee "trim")))))
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq pure_transformation_value)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language python
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call)))))
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq must_use_value)
                          (provenance eq native)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language rust
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call)))))
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq must_use_value)
                          (provenance eq native)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language cpp
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call))))))))
    (group :name by-call :by (discarded.id)
      (aggregate :name discarded-results :op count))
    (assert :group by-call :value discarded-results :cardinality (exactly 0))))
